    "slug": "student-hostels-legon-upsa-wisconsin-accra-2026",
    "title": "Best Student Hostels Around Legon, UPSA and Wisconsin in Accra 2026",
    "excerpt": "Looking for a hostel near University of Ghana Legon, UPSA or Wisconsin University? Here's your complete guide to student accommodation in Accra in 2026.",
    "date": "July 30, 2026",
    "readTime": "6 min read",
    "category": "Rental Guide",
    "content": "\n      <p>Finding affordable and safe student accommodation in Accra is one of the biggest challenges for university students. Whether you're studying at the University of Ghana (Legon), UPSA, Wisconsin International University or any other institution in Accra, this guide will help you find the best hostel options in 2026.</p>\n\n      <h2>Student Hostels Around University of Ghana, Legon</h2>\n      <p>Legon is home to Ghana's most prestigious university and has a vibrant student accommodation market. Here are the main areas and options:</p>\n\n      <h3>On-Campus Accommodation</h3>\n      <p>The University of Ghana has several on-campus halls of residence including Mensah Sarbah Hall, Akuafo Hall, Commonwealth Hall, Volta Hall and Legon Hall. On-campus accommodation is heavily subsidised and very affordable but spaces are extremely limited and priority is given to first-year and final-year students.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Cost: GHS 500–1,500 per semester</li>\n        <li>Apply through the university's online portal</li>\n        <li>Apply early — spaces fill up very fast</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h3>Off-Campus Hostels Near Legon</h3>\n      <p>Most students live off-campus in the surrounding communities. Popular areas include:</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Madina</strong> — very popular with Legon students, affordable and well-connected by trotro</li>\n        <li><strong>Adenta</strong> — slightly further but offers good value for money</li>\n        <li><strong>Haatso</strong> — close to Legon with affordable single and double rooms</li>\n        <li><strong>Atomic Junction</strong> — convenient location with good transport links</li>\n        <li><strong>Community 18 & 25</strong> — affordable areas popular with students</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h3>Typical Hostel Costs Near Legon</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Single room (shared bathroom)</strong> — GHS 1,500–3,000 per year</li>\n        <li><strong>Single room (self-contained)</strong> — GHS 3,000–6,000 per year</li>\n        <li><strong>Chamber and hall</strong> — GHS 2,500–5,000 per year</li>\n        <li><strong>Apartment (shared)</strong> — GHS 4,000–8,000 per year</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Student Hostels Around UPSA</h2>\n      <p>The University of Professional Studies Accra (UPSA) is located at Okponglo, East Legon. It's close to Legon and shares much of the same accommodation market.</p>\n\n      <h3>Best Areas for UPSA Students</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>East Legon</strong> — prestigious but expensive. Good for students with family support</li>\n        <li><strong>Madina</strong> — most popular choice for UPSA students, affordable and easy to commute</li>\n        <li><strong>Okponglo</strong> — walking distance to UPSA, several hostels available</li>\n        <li><strong>Adenta</strong> — affordable with regular transport to UPSA</li>\n        <li><strong>Kisseman</strong> — very affordable, popular with budget-conscious students</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h3>Typical Hostel Costs Near UPSA</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Single room (shared)</strong> — GHS 1,200–2,500 per year</li>\n        <li><strong>Self-contained room</strong> — GHS 2,500–5,000 per year</li>\n        <li><strong>Shared apartment</strong> — GHS 3,500–7,000 per year</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Student Hostels Around Wisconsin International University</h2>\n      <p>Wisconsin International University College Ghana is located at Okponglo, very close to UPSA and Legon. Students benefit from the same accommodation options available to Legon and UPSA students.</p>\n\n      <h3>Best Areas for Wisconsin Students</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Okponglo & Shiashie</strong> — closest to campus, walking distance</li>\n        <li><strong>Madina</strong> — affordable with regular trotro to campus</li>\n        <li><strong>East Legon Hills</strong> — newer developments with modern amenities</li>\n        <li><strong>Adenta</strong> — good value, 15–20 minutes by trotro</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>What to Look for in a Student Hostel</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Security</strong> — gated compound with security guard is essential</li>\n        <li><strong>Water supply</strong> — reliable water is critical. Ask about Ghana Water connection and storage tanks</li>\n        <li><strong>Electricity</strong> — prepaid meter is preferred so you control your bill</li>\n        <li><strong>Internet</strong> — fibre or strong mobile data signal for studying</li>\n        <li><strong>Kitchen</strong> — shared kitchen facilities save money on food</li>\n        <li><strong>Distance to campus</strong> — calculate transport costs in your budget</li>\n        <li><strong>Noise levels</strong> — visit at night to check for noise from bars or churches nearby</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Tips for Finding a Hostel in Accra as a Student</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Start early</strong> — good hostels fill up 2–3 months before semester starts</li>\n        <li><strong>Visit in person</strong> — never pay for accommodation you haven't physically seen</li>\n        <li><strong>Ask seniors</strong> — upperclassmen know the best and worst hostels near campus</li>\n        <li><strong>Check Facebook groups</strong> — \"UG Students\", \"UPSA Students\" and university WhatsApp groups often have hostel listings</li>\n        <li><strong>Use online platforms</strong> — <strong>Makola Digital</strong> lists student hostels and rooms for rent near all major universities in Accra</li>\n        <li><strong>Negotiate</strong> — landlords near universities expect negotiation especially if you're paying a full year upfront</li>\n        <li><strong>Read the agreement</strong> — understand what's included (water, electricity, security) before signing</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Red Flags to Avoid</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Landlord or agent asking for payment before viewing</li>\n        <li>No written tenancy agreement</li>\n        <li>Price far below market rate</li>\n        <li>Overcrowded rooms with too many students</li>\n        <li>No functioning toilet or bathroom facilities</li>\n        <li>Location that requires multiple transport connections late at night</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Find Student Accommodation on Makola Digital</h2>\n      <p>Browse student hostels, single rooms, self-contained rooms and shared apartments near Legon, UPSA, Wisconsin and other universities in Accra on Makola Digital. Connect directly with landlords — no agent fees, no hassle. Find your perfect student accommodation today.</p>\n    "
